 {:seon.task/name "the-entity-index-readers-take-only-the-entity-schemas-that-can-match"
  :seon.task/plan "Follow-up of the 2026-11-10 fix (seon.db/entity-index is a reader of the :seon.env/schemas class, seon.program/env-class-readers): sound, and coarse. About 1,160 of 1,614 tests reach the entity index, so any edit to resources/seon/schemas reruns 72% of the tests (599 before). Measured from git log: 196 of the 757 commits on main from 2026-10-27 to 2026-11-10 touched the schema resources (26%), so the coarse input costs often. A finer sound input: a reader of the entity index depends on the entity schemas that could win the match for what it asks, i.e. the entity schemas declaring an attribute its reach names (the membership measured that day as an edge, attribute -> entity row of the schema's text only: 631-1,124 tests moved per entity-schema edit, a render's body reached only through it missed) plus the schemas it names. Before building, measure per landing over a week: tests rerun by schema edits under the class rule against the finer rule, and whether any red the finer rule would have missed appears. Proof, red first: a test naming one entity's attributes keeps its digest when an unrelated entity schema changes, and moves when its own does."
